  _spoiledSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: be4b2c9711e2f524bb2ef25ae1305aec, type: 3}
  _plateSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 9fb9950b2b45c3b488176cb97cbf21de, type: 3}
  _isSmallIngredient: 1
  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: 'It does not get simpler than a piece of stretched
    out dough, grilled until the taste of raw flour does not immediately assault
    the mouth. This dish has been cooked, consumed and enjoyed for so long, one can
    only wonder how many civilizations, regimes, and nations that the concept of
    flatbread has witnessed. One thing shall hold true: a flatbread shall stand vigil
    as Verehn falls. Who knows, it might be the one on the grill right now...'
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: 'Alas, even the flatbread cannot stand for so long
    against the current of time. Its short vigil ends with a slow deterioration,
    peppered with fungal colonies spreading throughout its doughy body. However,
    a small slice of society enjoys the sharp bristles of these mold spots brushing
    against their palate, so it is a popular dish among these circles. If a society
    enjoys this variation: is it a twisted sign of their slow decay, or will they
    inherit the stalwart history of the flatbread in all of its forms?'
